00:13:07,459 --> 00:13:09,601
or a Frontier with a V six.

340
00:13:09,781 --> 00:13:11,789
Each one has a different strength.

341
00:13:11,969 --> 00:13:14,829
The Frontier's is simplicity and a growing

342
00:13:14,829 --> 00:13:15,510
following.

343
00:13:15,690 --> 00:13:18,546
The others have stronger numbers on resale

344
00:13:18,546 --> 00:13:19,498
and longevity.

345
00:13:19,849 --> 00:13:22,461
Now think about Nissan as a company.

346
00:13:22,641 --> 00:13:24,317
Through nine months,

347
00:13:24,317 --> 00:13:27,668
the Titan and the Frontier together sold

348
00:13:27,668 --> 00:13:31,941
sixty-six thousand, five hundred twenty-six trucks,

349
00:13:31,941 --> 00:13:33,868
up thirty-four percent.

350
00:13:34,048 --> 00:13:36,747
In our calculation from the Pickup Truck

351
00:13:36,747 --> 00:13:39,311
Talk table, Nissan went from about two

352
00:13:39,311 --> 00:13:41,605
point one percent of the trucks in

353
00:13:41,605 --> 00:13:43,899
that table to about two point nine

354
00:13:43,899 --> 00:13:44,439
percent.

355
00:13:44,619 --> 00:13:47,034
A gain of eight tenths of a

356
00:13:47,034 --> 00:13:49,181
point, in a flat market,

357
00:13:49,181 --> 00:13:51,597
is a large move for a small

358
00:13:51,597 --> 00:13:52,223
player.

359
00:13:52,573 --> 00:13:54,644
And the Titan is the other half

360
00:13:54,644 --> 00:13:55,580
of that story.

361
00:13:55,760 --> 00:13:58,730
It sold two thousand and twenty-four trucks

362
00:13:58,730 --> 00:14:01,631
through nine months of twenty twenty-five,

363
00:14:01,631 --> 00:14:03,980
and thirteen in twenty twenty-six.

364
00:14:04,160 --> 00:14:06,730
Nissan did not close the Canton plant

365
00:14:06,730 --> 00:14:08,397
when it ended the Titan.

366
00:14:08,577 --> 00:14:11,387
According to Motor Authority at the time,

367
00:14:11,387 --> 00:14:13,785
the company said no job losses were

368
00:14:13,785 --> 00:14:16,252
planned, and that the plant would be

369
00:14:16,252 --> 00:14:18,376
retooled for electric vehicles.

370
00:14:18,556 --> 00:14:20,270
So Nissan made a choice,

371
00:14:20,270 --> 00:14:22,628
to leave the big truck market and

372
00:14:22,628 --> 00:14:24,914
to put its truck effort into the

373
00:14:24,914 --> 00:14:25,557
Frontier.

374
00:14:25,907 --> 00:14:28,260
Whether that choice is right will take

375
00:14:28,260 --> 00:14:29,065
years to see.

376
00:14:29,245 --> 00:14:31,689
A midsize truck can grow quickly,

377
00:14:31,689 --> 00:14:33,986
but it is a smaller market than

378
00:14:33,986 --> 00:14:35,542
the full-size trucks,

379
00:14:35,542 --> 00:14:38,060
which sold more than one point six

380
00:14:38,060 --> 00:14:40,135
million through nine months.

381
00:14:40,315 --> 00:14:43,826
The Frontier's gain of nearly nineteen thousand

382
00:14:43,826 --> 00:14:44,947
trucks is real.

383
00:14:45,127 --> 00:14:47,863
But it equals only about one percent

384
00:14:47,863 --> 00:14:50,828
of the number of full-size trucks sold.

385
00:14:51,008 --> 00:14:53,027
A company that wants to be a

386
00:14:53,027 --> 00:14:55,768
major truck maker needs a bigger truck

387
00:14:55,768 --> 00:14:56,778
than this one.

388
00:14:57,128 --> 00:14:59,380
The last twist is about who should

389
00:14:59,380 --> 00:15:00,971
buy the Frontier anyway.

390
00:15:01,151 --> 00:15:03,288
A buyer who wants a simple,

391
00:15:03,288 --> 00:15:05,346
naturally aspirated V six,

392
00:15:05,346 --> 00:15:08,274
a truck that tows over seven thousand

393
00:15:08,274 --> 00:15:10,649
pounds, and a price in the low

394
00:15:10,649 --> 00:15:12,865
thirties, has a good reason.

395
00:15:13,045 --> 00:15:15,195
A buyer who plans to keep the

396
00:15:15,195 --> 00:15:17,272
truck for ten years or more,

397
00:15:17,272 --> 00:15:19,274
and not worry about resale,

398
00:15:19,274 --> 00:15:22,017
can also decide that the lower resale

399
00:15:22,017 --> 00:15:23,204
does not matter.

400
00:15:23,384 --> 00:15:25,778
The numbers are about the market,

401
00:15:25,778 --> 00:15:27,157
not about your use.

402
00:15:27,507 --> 00:15:29,705
And a buyer who plans to sell

403
00:15:29,705 --> 00:15:32,661
in five years should compare carefully.

404
00:15:32,841 --> 00:15:35,556
Ask the dealer for the out-the-door price,

405
00:15:35,556 --> 00:15:37,172
with the destination fee.

406
00:15:37,352 --> 00:15:39,659
Ask for the price of the Tacoma,

407
00:15:39,659 --> 00:15:42,111
the Colorado and the Ranger at the

408
00:15:42,111 --> 00:15:42,832
same time.

409
00:15:43,012 --> 00:15:45,378
And use the fifteen dollar gap with

410
00:15:45,378 --> 00:15:47,609
the Tacoma as a reminder that you

411
00:15:47,609 --> 00:15:49,908
are not buying the cheapest truck.

412
00:15:50,088 --> 00:15:51,725
You are buying a truck at a

413
00:15:51,725 --> 00:15:53,969
price where the market gives you many

414
00:15:53,969 --> 00:15:54,454
choices.

415
00:15:54,804 --> 00:15:57,073
Let us slow down on the fifteen

416
00:15:57,073 --> 00:15:59,489
dollar gap, because it is easy to

417
00:15:59,489 --> 00:16:00,075
misread.

418
00:16:00,255 --> 00:16:02,963
Fifteen dollars is less than the thirty

419
00:16:02,963 --> 00:16:06,365
dollar disagreement between the sources about the

420
00:16:06,365 --> 00:16:07,476
destination fee.

421
00:16:07,656 --> 00:16:09,702
So the gap is smaller than the

422
00:16:09,702 --> 00:16:10,930
noise in the data.

423
00:16:11,110 --> 00:16:13,230
It does not mean the Frontier is

424
00:16:13,230 --> 00:16:14,291
the better deal,

425
00:16:14,291 --> 00:16:16,345
and it does not mean the Tacoma

426
00:16:16,345 --> 00:16:16,543
is.

427
00:16:16,723 --> 00:16:18,657
It means that on the sticker,

428
00:16:18,657 --> 00:16:20,257
the two trucks are tied,

429
00:16:20,257 --> 00:16:22,457
and the decision has to come from

430
00:16:22,457 --> 00:16:23,457
somewhere else.

431
00:16:23,808 --> 00:16:25,921
So where should the decision come from?

432
00:16:26,101 --> 00:16:27,822
Start with what you do with the

433
00:16:27,822 --> 00:16:28,156
truck.

434
00:16:28,336 --> 00:16:30,836
The Frontier offers a V six with

435
00:16:30,836 --> 00:16:33,103
three hundred ten horsepower,

436
00:16:33,103 --> 00:16:35,682
and it tows up to seven thousand,

437
00:16:35,682 --> 00:16:37,635
one hundred fifty pounds.

438
00:16:37,815 --> 00:16:41,134
The Tacoma offers a turbo four-cylinder and

439
00:16:41,134 --> 00:16:43,527
a hybrid with much more torque.

440
00:16:43,707 --> 00:16:46,129
If you value a simple engine,

441
00:16:46,129 --> 00:16:47,632
the Frontier fits.

442
00:16:47,812 --> 00:16:50,070
If you value the most torque and

443
00:16:50,070 --> 00:16:51,199
the best resale,

444
00:16:51,199 --> 00:16:53,245
the numbers favor the Tacoma.

445
00:16:53,425 --> 00:16:55,201
Neither answer is wrong.

446
00:16:55,381 --> 00:16:57,111
They are different priorities.

447
00:16:57,461 --> 00:17:00,234
Now let us explain the resale number

448
00:17:00,234 --> 00:17:01,389
in plain words,

449
00:17:01,389 --> 00:17:04,009
because it is the one buyers skip.

450
00:17:04,189 --> 00:17:07,491
Sixty-three point four percent after five years

451
00:17:07,491 --> 00:17:10,301
means that for every hundred dollars you

452
00:17:10,301 --> 00:17:12,760
pay today, the truck is worth about

453
00:17:12,760 --> 00:17:15,149
sixty-three dollars when you sell.

454
00:17:15,329 --> 00:17:17,953
The Tacoma, at eighty and a half

455
00:17:17,953 --> 00:17:20,495
percent, is worth about eighty.

456
00:17:20,675 --> 00:17:23,032
That gap is not a small detail.

457
00:17:23,212 --> 00:17:25,517
It is money that leaves your pocket

458
00:17:25,517 --> 00:17:27,427
slowly, a little every month,

459
00:17:27,427 --> 00:17:29,667
whether or not you ever notice it.

460
00:17:30,017 --> 00:17:32,601
A common mistake is to compare trucks

461
00:17:32,601 --> 00:17:34,208
by the monthly payment.

462
00:17:34,388 --> 00:17:37,018
A payment can look low because the

463
00:17:37,018 --> 00:17:38,024
loan is long,

464
00:17:38,024 --> 00:17:40,422
and it hides both the price and

465
00:17:40,422 --> 00:17:41,273
the resale.

466
00:17:41,453 --> 00:17:43,976
A better habit is to compare three

467
00:17:43,976 --> 00:17:45,609
things on every truck.

468
00:17:45,789 --> 00:17:47,350
The out-the-door price,

469
00:17:47,350 --> 00:17:49,725
which includes the destination fee.

470
00:17:49,905 --> 00:17:52,296
The five-year resale percentage.

471
00:17:52,476 --> 00:17:54,423
And the tow rating for the exact

472
00:17:54,423 --> 00:17:55,274
trim you want.

473
00:17:55,454 --> 00:17:57,464
If a dealer will not give you

474
00:17:57,464 --> 00:17:59,889
all three, that is information too.

475
00:18:00,240 --> 00:18:02,702
Here is how to verify the destination

476
00:18:02,702 --> 00:18:02,968
fee.

477
00:18:03,148 --> 00:18:05,558
Ask the dealer to write down the

478
00:18:05,558 --> 00:18:07,140
full price in a list,

479
00:18:07,140 --> 00:18:08,119
line by line,

480
00:18:08,119 --> 00:18:09,851
with the sticker price,

481
00:18:09,851 --> 00:18:11,357
the destination fee,

482
00:18:11,357 --> 00:18:14,144
taxes and any dealer fees on separate

483
00:18:14,144 --> 00:18:14,595
lines.

484
00:18:14,775 --> 00:18:18,232
Our sources gave seventeen forty-five and seventeen

485
00:18:18,232 --> 00:18:21,282
seventy-five dollars, and they could not both

486
00:18:21,282 --> 00:18:21,892
be right.

487
00:18:22,072 --> 00:18:23,872
The written list settles it.

488
00:18:24,052 --> 00:18:25,608
If a line is vague,

489
00:18:25,608 --> 00:18:27,165
ask what it is for,

490
00:18:27,165 --> 00:18:29,950
and ask whether it can be removed.

491
00:18:30,300 --> 00:18:33,126
Remember also that the sales growth tells

492
00:18:33,126 --> 00:18:34,504
you what buyers did,

493
00:18:34,504 --> 00:18:36,572
not what the truck will do for

494
00:18:36,572 --> 00:18:36,848
you.

495
00:18:37,028 --> 00:18:40,321
The Frontier is up thirty-nine point six

496
00:18:40,321 --> 00:18:42,461
percent, and that is real.

497
00:18:42,641 --> 00:18:44,761
But a truck can be popular for

498
00:18:44,761 --> 00:18:47,092
a good price and still lose value

499
00:18:47,092 --> 00:18:47,587
faster.

500
00:18:47,767 --> 00:18:50,530
Popularity is a fact about the market.

501
00:18:50,710 --> 00:18:54,460
Resale and longevity are facts about ownership.

502
00:18:54,640 --> 00:18:57,423
When a video or a salesperson quotes

503
00:18:57,423 --> 00:18:59,356
the first kind of number,

504
00:18:59,356 --> 00:19:01,211
ask for the second kind.

505
00:19:01,562 --> 00:19:04,009
Let us be fair to the Frontier,

506
00:19:04,009 --> 00:19:04,325
too.

507
00:19:04,505 --> 00:19:08,426
The longevity numbers describe averages across many

508
00:19:08,426 --> 00:19:10,194
trucks, not your truck.

509
00:19:10,374 --> 00:19:14,286
A well-maintained truck with regular oil changes

510
00:19:14,286 --> 00:19:15,998
can beat the average,

511
00:19:15,998 --> 00:19:18,361
and a neglected one will not.

512
00:19:18,541 --> 00:19:20,933
The study cannot see how you drive.

513
00:19:21,113 --> 00:19:23,230
So the right way to use the

514
00:19:23,230 --> 00:19:25,975
twelve and a half percent figure is

515
00:19:25,975 --> 00:19:28,171
as a reason to look closely,

516
00:19:28,171 --> 00:19:30,602
to ask for service records on a

517
00:19:30,602 --> 00:19:33,503
used truck, and to keep a maintenance

518
00:19:33,503 --> 00:19:34,836
log on a new one.

519
00:19:35,186 --> 00:19:37,969
Finally, think about the buyer who should

520
00:19:37,969 --> 00:19:38,309
wait.

521
00:19:38,489 --> 00:19:40,533
If you plan to sell in five

522
00:19:40,533 --> 00:19:43,031
years, or if you need the highest

523
00:19:43,031 --> 00:19:44,469
resale you can get,

524
00:19:44,469 --> 00:19:47,270
give the Tacoma a serious look before

525
00:19:47,270 --> 00:19:47,951
you sign.

526
00:19:48,131 --> 00:19:50,880
If Toyota has not yet published its

527
00:19:50,880 --> 00:19:53,000
twenty twenty-seven prices,

528
00:19:53,000 --> 00:19:54,413
as Autoblog noted,

529
00:19:54,413 --> 00:19:57,162
you can wait and compare again when

530
00:19:57,162 --> 00:19:57,790
it does.

531
00:19:57,970 --> 00:20:00,113
And if you decide on the Frontier

532
00:20:00,113 --> 00:20:02,839
anyway, you now know exactly which numbers

533
00:20:02,839 --> 00:20:04,008
you are accepting.

534
00:20:04,358 --> 00:20:07,361
One last practical tip for any midsize

535
00:20:07,361 --> 00:20:08,468
truck shopper.

536
00:20:08,648 --> 00:20:10,438
Do not let the order of the

537
00:20:10,438 --> 00:20:12,560
conversation decide the outcome.

538
00:20:12,740 --> 00:20:15,886
Many buyers talk about the monthly payment

539
00:20:15,886 --> 00:20:17,758
first, then the trade-in,

540
00:20:17,758 --> 00:20:18,882
then the price.

541
00:20:19,062 --> 00:20:19,886
Reverse it.

542
00:20:20,066 --> 00:20:22,426
Settle the price of the truck first,

543
00:20:22,426 --> 00:20:25,442
in writing, with the destination fee included.

544
00:20:25,622 --> 00:20:27,790
Then talk about the trade-in as a

545
00:20:27,790 --> 00:20:28,710
separate deal.

546
00:20:28,890 --> 00:20:30,631
Then talk about financing.

547
00:20:30,811 --> 00:20:34,197
Three separate negotiations are easier to check

548
00:20:34,197 --> 00:20:35,998
than one big tangled one,

549
00:20:35,998 --> 00:20:38,591
and each number can be compared with

550
00:20:38,591 --> 00:20:40,680
the figures we covered today.

551
00:20:41,030 --> 00:20:43,061
So what should you check before you

552
00:20:43,061 --> 00:20:45,558
buy a midsize truck in twenty twenty-seven?

553
00:20:45,738 --> 00:20:49,350
First, the out-the-door price with the destination

554
00:20:49,350 --> 00:20:49,639
fee.

555
00:20:49,819 --> 00:20:52,495
Second, the engine and the towing for

556
00:20:52,495 --> 00:20:53,580
the exact trim.

557
00:20:53,760 --> 00:20:56,345
Third, the five-year resale value,

558
00:20:56,345 --> 00:20:59,310
which is where the Frontier is weakest.

559
00:20:59,490 --> 00:21:02,331
And fourth, whether the model is still

560
00:21:02,331 --> 00:21:03,228
being built.

561
00:21:03,408 --> 00:21:05,182
We put all of this into a

562
00:21:05,182 --> 00:21:09,085
checklist, the Twenty Twenty-Seven Truck Buyer's Guide.

